Reason: a precise collision test scans every sample of the two boxes' overlap until one lands on a set pixel of both
masks. A power bomb's blast is a growing circle whose box covers dozens of walls, and the walls in the box's corners
lie outside the circle: each got a full scan that could not hit (in the mine room, with the chain running, the power
bomb's collision with the walls took up to ~5 ms a frame on the Wii). Each mask frame now records how far from the
sprite's origin a sample landing on one of its set pixels can be (computed once, on first use); when the overlap's
closest sample is farther from the instance than that, scaled by the larger of its scale factors, plus a margin, no
sample can hit and the scan is skipped. Rotation keeps distances, so it needs no special case.
Upstream: Speed only, every platform. Retires this patch when merged.

